{
 "name": "tiny_plumbing",
 "description": "The tiny tier: random-weight pipelines from hf-internal-testing (public, 1 to 56 MB each, local copies under $WORKSPACE/hf_tiny/<name>) through Studio in process, Studio over HTTP and plain diffusers. Every cell takes seconds; run it on EVERY change as plumbing: loads, family routing, quant / offload / cache / compile code paths, video export, the HTTP route. Output is noise: never quote a pixel or a timing from it, and the AMD criteria judge tiny cells on broken / newly flagged only. Sizes are per model: Studio refuses images under 256 px (MIN_OUTPUT_SIDE), tiny Z-Image's rope overflows at 256 so it runs through the diffusers backend at 64, tiny Wan runs at 64x64x9 (video has no 256 floor). Tiny Wan emits blank frames by construction (flagged at every state, so never a regression). Known on the wt_offload_pin tree: FBCache does not engage on tiny Qwen-Image-2.1 (read status.transformer_cache), compile fails on tiny Wan (dynamo fake-tensor SDPA error, so the Wan cells stay at speed off), transformer_cache static is refused on trees without PR 11737. Edit pipelines (tiny-flux-kontext-pipe, tiny-qwenimage-edit-pipe) need an input image and are left to the edge suite; tiny Sana / HunyuanVideo / CogVideoX failed in plain diffusers at 64 px (device assert / size mismatch) and are left out.",
 "models": {
  "tiny_flux_pipe": {
   "repo": "hf-internal-testing/tiny-flux-pipe",
   "local": "$WORKSPACE/hf_tiny/tiny-flux-pipe"
  },
  "tiny_lumina2_pipe": {
   "repo": "hf-internal-testing/tiny-lumina2-pipe",
   "local": "$WORKSPACE/hf_tiny/tiny-lumina2-pipe"
  },
  "tiny_qwenimage21_pipe": {
